<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pancasila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pancasila is the official philosophy of the Indonesian state, set out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> in a speech of 1 June 1945. Its five principles are belief in one God, just and civilised humanity, the unity of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, democracy guided by deliberation and consensus, and social justice for all Indonesians. It is written into the preamble of the 1945 constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pancasila.jpg" alt="Pancasila" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Indonesia (uncredited) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garuda_Pancasila_Poster_(color).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
